{"type": "message", "id": "03d93390", "parentId": "83d12384", "timestamp": "2026-08-17T17:25:13.488Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Your connected mouse is a **Logitech MX Master 3S** (Bluetooth BLE), not USB.\n\nNeither macOS system tools nor USB descriptors will report polling rate here \u2014 it's a Bluetooth BLE connection, and macOS doesn't expose HID report rate/polling frequency for BLE or USB devices via any CLI. That info comes only from Logitech's own spec sheet or Logi Options+ software.\n\nPer Logitech's published specs, the **MX Master 3S over Bluetooth LE polls at ~125 Hz** (8ms); if paired via the Logi Bolt USB receiver instead, it can reach up to 1000 Hz. I can't verify which mode you're actually using right now beyond confirming it's connected via Bluetooth (not a Bolt receiver, since no such USB dongle appears in the USB list)."}], "api": "anthropic-messages", "provider": "anthropic", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "usage": {"input": 2, "output": 282, "cacheRead": 17010, "cacheWrite": 3526, "totalTokens": 20820, "cost": {"input": 4e-06, "output": 0.00282, "cacheRead": 0.0034020000000000005, "cacheWrite": 0.008815, "total": 0.015041}, "cacheWrite1h": 0, "reasoning": 0}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1786987508423, "responseId": "msg_011Ce8iBTFJLpPe1C9J7BGWX", "rawStopReason": "end_turn"}}
